    pr_ref:  # 60c0
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-28 closing WI-johib (PR #1279). ruby's _try_receiver_call tries a scope_resolution receiver's SHORT NAME as a candidate (Prometheus::Client -> 'Client'), and ruby symbol names carry no namespace (a class Client in any module is named 'Client'). So an EXTERNAL namespaced constant whose last segment matches a project class is treated as that class. Measured on postal after #1279: Prometheus::Client.registry -> project Client -> the inherited-calls linker -> HasPrometheusMetrics.registry, a wrong binding (1 site on postal; 0 on chatwoot).\n\nFIX SHAPE (not built): take the short-name candidate only when the full name cannot be external. For example, require that the leading namespace segment ('Prometheus') is itself a project module, or record the namespace on class symbols (meta) and compare it. Measure on postal and chatwoot. WI-surar (the lowercased module slot) is adjacent: it is about the external spelling, not the binding."  # 60c0
    fields: {}  # 60c0
